---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { site, contact } from '../config/site';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Cookie policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`${site.domain} sets no cookies and runs no analytics.`}
  lastUpdated="21 August 2026"
>
  <div class="mb-10 rounded-[2px] border border-rule bg-accent-wash p-5 text-accent-ink">
    <p class="text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="font-semibold">Draft pending legal review.</strong> This
      page describes the site as currently built. If analytics or any embedded
      third-party content is added later, it must be updated &mdash; and a
      consent banner will be required.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    {site.domain} sets <strong>no cookies</strong>. We run no analytics, no
    advertising pixels, no session tracking and no embedded third-party
    content. There is nothing here to consent to, which is why you were not
    asked.
  </p>

  <h2>What that means in practice</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No first-party cookies.</strong> The site is static. It has no
      login, no shopping basket and no personalisation, so it has nothing to
      remember about you between visits.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No analytics.</strong> We do not measure your visit. We have no
      idea which pages you read.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No third-party embeds.</strong> Fonts are self-hosted from our own
      domain rather than loaded from a font CDN, so no external service sees
      your request.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No advertising or social tracking.</strong> Links to LinkedIn are
      ordinary links. Nothing is loaded from social platforms until you click
      through.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What still happens without cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Two things involve a third party, neither of which uses cookies to track
    you:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Form submissions.</strong> When you submit a form, its contents
      are sent to Web3Forms, which delivers them to our mailbox. This happens
      only when you press Send.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host records standard technical request
      data for security and reliability, as described in the{' '}
      <a href={withBase('/privacy')}>privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your browser&rsquo;s local storage</h2>
  <p>
    We do not write to <code>localStorage</code>, <code>sessionStorage</code> or
    IndexedDB either.
  </p>

  <h2>If this changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we ever add analytics, we will use a cookieless, privacy-preserving
    provider where possible, update this page, and add a consent banner if the
    provider requires one. Questions:{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${contact.general}`}>{contact.general}</a>.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
